sulin, necessitating continuous management of insulin and blood glucose levels. Additionally, Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1 poses a higher risk for developing eating disorders, particularly in young women, which can complicate the careful management required for the condition. Overall, DM1 demands vigilant monitoring and a comprehensive approach to treatment to maintain health and mitigate associated risks.", "HYPERCALORIC DIABETES-SPECIFIC ENTERAL NUTRITIONAL FORMULA:A specialized nutritional formula designed for patients with diabetes to improve their nutritional status and glycemic control.", "DIABETES TECHNOLOGY:Diabetes technology refers to the tools and methods used to manage diabetes, including enteral formulas and monitoring devices.", "DIABETES MELLITUS TYPE 1:Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 (DM1) is an autoimmune disease characterized by chronic insulin deficiency. This condition necessitates careful management of diet and physical activity to effectively control blood sugar levels. It is a chronic condition that can lead to various complications, and in this particular case, it was diagnosed in the patient at the age of 28.", "AMERICAN PSYCHIATRIC ASSOCIATION:The American Psychiatric Association is a professional organization that publishes the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders (DSM-5), which includes criteria for diagnosing eating disorders.", "FUNDACIÓN SED:The Fundación SED is an organization in Spain that provides data and support for individuals with diabetes, including statistics on the prevalence of diabetes in minors.", "ANOREXIA NERVIOSA:Anorexia Nervosa is an eating disorder marked by an intense fear of gaining weight and a distorted body image, leading to severe food restriction and health risks.", "TRASTORNO DE EVITACIÓN/RESTRICCIÓN DE ALIMENTOS:Avoidant/Restrictive Food Intake Disorder is characterized by a lack of interest in eating or avoidance of certain foods, which can lead to nutritional deficiencies.", "TRASTORNO DE ATRACONES:Binge Eating Disorder involves recurrent episodes of eating large quantities of food, often to the point of discomfort, and is associated with feelings of loss of control.", "PICA:Pica is an eating disorder characterized by the persistent consumption of non-nutritive, non-food substances, which can lead to serious health complications.", "TRASTORNO DE RUMIACIÓN:Rumination Disorder involves the repeated regurgitation of food, which may be re-chewed, re-swallowed, or spit out, and can have significant health implications.", "CIE-9:The International Classification of Diseases, 9th Revision (ICD-9) is a system used for coding and classifying diseases, including eating disorders.", "CIE-10:The International Classification of Diseases, 10th Revision (ICD-10) is an updated system for coding diseases, providing guidelines for the classification of eating disorders."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}